      "writtenOn": "2023-07-05T12:05:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mainline updatable modules are shipped by Google via the play store and are signed by Google certificates, and are thus com.google... for example com.google.android.tethering\n\nBasically for mainline updatability:\n- the code must be modular (ie. use APIs into the rest of the system)\n- it must be built in a way that enables updates\n  - ie. either APK or \u0027normal\u0027 APEX, but *not* \u0027flattened APEX\u0027, ...\n- it must be signed by a Google certificate, and present in the playstore in that fashion.",
      "parentUuid": "9331e916_757aa052",
      "revId": "7fc2fcd6b4b56650edde81ce9e2bf94b415e7a3d",
